; WO-0046 Phase 1 — the co-simulation lane's tb_writer half (§2.1, §2.2).
;
; (executables), deliberately NOT (inline_tests): `compare` depends on a file
; `vvp` produces, and `vvp` runs outside dune and does not exist in any
; environment where the lane has not been run — including this dev
; container, including every existing CI job that does not carry iverilog.
; An inline test here would fail the MAIN suite everywhere iverilog is
; absent. `dune build @default` builds these three binaries wherever a real
; Hardcaml toolchain is present (which `ours_run` genuinely needs, to
; elaborate M03); `dune runtest` never touches them, because nothing here is
; wired to the `runtest` alias — no `(rule (alias runtest) ...)`, unlike
; test/cost_probe/dune's throwaway probe. The main suite's fifteen
; %expect_test units are therefore untouched by this stanza either way.
;
; iverilog is not invoked from here at all: tools/cosim/run_cosim.sh
; (data_wrangler, WO-0046 §5) is the only thing that calls `iverilog`/`vvp`,
; against test/cosim/tb_xgmii_rx_64.v plus the two vendored files under
; test/third_party/verilog-ethernet/.
;
; canonical.ml/.mli (WO-0046 §2.3's pinned grammar, writer/parser/comparison)
; and stimulus_gen.ml need no Hardcaml dependency at all -- the former is
; plain stdlib text processing, the latter drives only the DUT-independent
; dv_xgmii link-partner model. ours_run.ml is the one file here that touches
; Hardcaml_ethernet.Xgmii_rx_64, through the same Cyclesim.With_interface
; entry point and field-name projection test/xgmii_rx_64/bench.ml already
; uses (libs/hardcaml_ethernet/src/ and rtl_snapshots/** were not opened to
; write it, PROTOCOL §10). compare.ml depends on nothing beyond canonical.ml
; and the standard library, on purpose, so the comparator itself never needs
; a working Hardcaml toolchain to build or to run --self-test.

(executables
 (names stimulus_gen ours_run compare)
 (libraries hardcaml hardcaml_ethernet dv_xgmii dv_xgmii_probe dv_axi64_probe dv_monitors))
